    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Libertine is the fourth and final studio album by English rock band Gene, released in 2001 on the band’s own Contra label. It arrived after the group had been dropped by Polydor and captures a more stripped-back, reflective mood than their earlier, more openly anthemic Britpop records.\n\nMusically, the album keeps Gene’s gift for melodic, emotionally direct songwriting but leans into a darker, more restrained rock sound, with songs like “Is It Over?” and “O Lover” highlighting Martin Rossiter’s expressive vocal style. Reception was mixed at the time, though later listeners and critics often regard it as an underrated late-period statement, valued for its seriousness, cohesion, and sense of farewell.",
